ps://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/deployments","created_at":"2016-10-14T12:27:49Z","updated_at":"2026-10-31T16:52:02Z","pushed_at":"2026-07-24T07:39:04Z","git_url":"git://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:RasaHQ/rasa.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa","homepage":"https://rasa.com/docs/rasa/","size":1707110,"stargazers_count":21364,"watchers_count":21364,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":4914,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":160,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["bot","bot-framework","botkit","bots","chatbot","chatbots","chatbots-framework","conversation-driven-development","conversational-agents","conversational-ai","conversational-bots","machine-learning","machine-learning-library","mitie","natural-language-processing","nlp","nlu","rasa","spacy","wit"],"visibility":"public","forks":4914,"open_issues":160,"watchers":21364,"default_branch":"3.6.x"},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/pulls/10295","html_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/10295","diff_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/10295.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/10295.patch","merged_at":"2021-11-30T09:50:36Z"},"body":"**Proposed changes**:\r\n- Fixes https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/10235\r\n- This PR fixes 2 issues:\r\n\r\n1. Initial issue of zombie slots after `/restart`: FormAction was checking all tracker events from the beginning. Coupled with the fact that UserUtterance has `__eq__` defined so that two messages with same content (such as `hi` - entities etc. are also equal) are taken to be equal, this meant that all events after the first message were taken into consideration, and `restart` events are also ignored. This bug only shows itself when there are duplicate messages and a `restart` event, and this is because slots are linked to unique forms and that once a form is filled in (slots filled) you cannot activate it again. Solution to the problem was searching in tracker store from the end, and also stopping at `RestartedEvent`. Slots are filled from then on.\r\n\r\n2. After implementing fix above, `test_formbot_example` was failing at this line: https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/runs/4289441802?check_suite_focus=true\r\n\r\n  - The `AssertionError` was caused because all form slots were filled so there was nothing to set afterwards, and that resulted in form rejection and the next action prediction was `action_default_fallback`.\r\n  - Upon further inspection of `tracker.events`, we realised that slot `preferences` got set after the `/restart`  user utterance because the original slot mapping conditions were satisfied - the `tracker.active_loop` was the same and the `requested_slot` was `preferences` while intent `restart` was allowed. This was fixed, by adding `restart` to the `not_intent` [list](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/blob/747a7b8e137fc9eee32248d6e638dd127a239ac2/examples/formbot/domain.yml#L64) in the slot mapping.\r\n  - We also realised that `outdoor_seating` got set immediately after [another unhappy path](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/blob/747a7b8e137fc9eee32248d6e638dd127a239ac2/tests/core/test_examples.py#L121), i.e, the sequence of user utterance `stop` -> bot action `utter_ask_continue`  -> user utterance `affirm` , because the form was still active, `requested_slot`  was `outdoor_seating` , intent was `affirm` and therefore all conditions in the slot [mapping](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/blob/747a7b8e137fc9eee32248d6e638dd127a239ac2/examples/formbot/domain.yml#L41) were satisfied. In order to prevent this slot to be set during an unhappy path, we added the 2nd fix in `ActionExtractSlots.run()` - this approach for checking for `LOOP_REJECTED` was required because the event `LoopInterrupted` got added to `tracker.events` after `SlotSet(outdoor_seating, True)` event. We couldn't quite figure out why `LoopInterrupted` doesn't get immediately added to `tracker.events` after the `stop` user utterance and instead `MemoizationPolicy` selects `utter_ask_continue`.\r\n\r\nActions for step 2 above have taken while pair programming with @ancalita \r\n\r\n**Status (please check what you already did)**:\r\n- [x] added some tests for the functionality\r\n- [x] updated the changelog (please check [changelog](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/tree/main/changelog) for instructions)\r\n- [x] reformat files using `black` (please check [Readme](https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa#code-style) for instructions)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/10295/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/10295/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/comments/974463851","html_url":"https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/10235#issuecomment-974463851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/10235","id":974463851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBDn5MM46FSNr","user":{"login":"tayfun","id":55836,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1ODM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55836?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun","html_url":"https://github.com/tayfun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-19T20:51:26Z","updated_at":"2021-11-19T20:51:59Z","body":"I think I found the core of the problem, but before that, I want to note that I see some duplicate events. For example, for the above playback, I see two events in tracker store which have the same exact slot set events for the single user utterance. Eg.\r\n```\r\n    {\r\n      \"event\": \"user\",\r\n      \"timestamp\": 1637330172.321048,\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"model_id\": \"37e752418f6f45a28cb94110449d5876\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"text\": \"Prague\",\r\n      \"parse_data\": {\r\n        \"intent\": {\r\n          \"name\": \"inform\",\r\n          \"confidence\": 0.9999785423278809\r\n        },\r\n        \"entities\": [\r\n          {\r\n            \"entity\": \"city\",\r\n            \"start\": 0,\r\n            \"end\": 6,\r\n            \"confidence_entity\": 0.9990973472595215,\r\n            \"value\": \"Prague\",\r\n            \"extractor\": \"DIETClassifier\"\r\n          }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"text\": \"Prague\",\r\n        \"message_id\": \"8b98c13dbb9b4745b637e8f8fd67d393\",\r\n        \"metadata\": {},\r\n        \"text_tokens\": [\r\n          [\r\n            0,\r\n            6\r\n          ]\r\n        ],\r\n        \"intent_ranking\": [\r\n          {\r\n            \"name\": \"inform\",\r\n            \"confidence\": 0.9999785423278809\r\n          },],\r\n        \"response_selector\": {\r\n          \"all_retrieval_intents\": [],\r\n          \"default\": {\r\n            \"response\": {\r\n              \"responses\": null,\r\n              \"confidence\": 0,\r\n              \"intent_response_key\": null,\r\n              \"utter_action\": \"utter_None\"\r\n            },\r\n            \"ranking\": []\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      \"input_channel\": \"cmdline\",\r\n      \"message_id\": \"8b98c13dbb9b4745b637e8f8fd67d393\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"event\": \"slot\",\r\n      \"timestamp\": 1637330172.3216739,\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"model_id\": \"37e752418f6f45a28cb94110449d5876\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"name\": \"slot_0\",\r\n      \"value\": \"Prague\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"event\": \"user_featurization\",\r\n      \"timestamp\": 1637330172.3262131,\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"model_id\": \"37e752418f6f45a28cb94110449d5876\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"use_text_for_featurization\": false\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"event\": \"action\",\r\n      \"timestamp\": 1637330172.3262231,\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"model_id\": \"37e752418f6f45a28cb94110449d5876\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"name\": \"my_form\",\r\n      \"policy\": \"RulePolicy\",\r\n      \"confidence\": 1,\r\n      \"action_text\": null,\r\n      \"hide_rule_turn\": true\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"event\": \"slot\",\r\n      \"timestamp\": 1637330172.3263,\r\n      \"metadata\": {\r\n        \"model_id\": \"37e752418f6f45a28cb94110449d5876\"\r\n      },\r\n      \"name\": \"slot_0\",\r\n      \"value\": \"Prague\"\r\n    },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow the core problem might be related to above so once a test and a fix is there, we should check above again. The problem right now is that we assume two UserUttered events are same if they have text,intent,entities and then in `FormAction._get_events_since_last_user_uttered` we check if it UserUttered is already in the dialogue tracker and its index using that equality. That is, if we have two `hi` messages like above, we'll start from the first one and use all the SlotSet events since then. See my comments in https://github.com/RasaHQ/rasa/pull/10295/files\r\n\r\n@ancalita I would probably need your help in fixing this :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/comments/974463851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"tayfun","id":55836,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1ODM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55836?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun","html_url":"https://github.com/tayfun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tayfun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":5647665125,"node_id":"MEE_lADOBDn5MM4-3raGzwAAAAFQoIfl","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RasaHQ/rasa/issues/events/5647665125","actor":{"login":"ancalita","id":27920906,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3OTIwOTA2","avatar_url":"https://